&Q000566 = Letter from Sîn-iddinam to the god Utu
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.2.05
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.2.05&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. {d}utu lugal-ŋu₁₀-ur₂ di-kud mah# an ki
#tr.en: Say to @wDN{Utu} my lord, the exalted judge of heaven and earth, who cares for the Land, who renders verdicts; just god, who loves to keep man alive, who heeds entreaty, who extends mercy, who knows …… compassion, who loves justice, who selects honesty, ……:
#lem: Utu[1]DN; lugal[king]; dikud[judge]; mah[great]; an[sky]; ki[place]
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. saŋ en₃# tar kalam-ma ka-aš mu-un#-bar-bar-re
#lem: saŋ[head]; en[cvne]; tar[cut]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; kaš[decision]; bar[place outside]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. diŋir zid lu₂ til₃-le-de₃ ki aŋ₂ a-ra-zu ŋiš tuku
#lem: diŋir[deity]; zid[right]; lu[person]; til[live (of a single person)]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; arazu[supplication]; ŋeš[tree]; tuku[acquire]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. arhuš sud šag₄# gur#-ru# mu-un-[...]-zu-[...]
#lem: arhuš[compassion]; sud[distant]; šag[heart]; gur[turn]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. niŋ₂-si-sa₂ ki aŋ₂ niŋ₂-zid [bar] tam#-me NE [...] U₃# [...] dug₄
#lem: niŋsisa[justice]; ki[place]; aŋ[measure]; niŋzid[righteousness]; bar[outside]; tam[clean]; X; X; X; X; dug[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. sun₄ mu₂ dumu# {d}nin-gal sun₄ {na₄}za-gin₃ X X X [...]
#tr.en: Repeat to the bearded one, the son of @wDN{Ningal}, …… a lapis-lazuli beard, @varh[t3205.v1]{who opens the bolts of heaven and earth } @vart[t3205.v2,t3205.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} who opens the bolts }, who creates brightness in darkness; foremost lord who alone is resplendent, whose greatness is unequalled; warrior, son given birth by @wDN{Ningal}, who guards and gathers together the divine powers; just god, prince who determines all the fates, my lord, father of the black-headed: this is what @wRN{@wDN{Sîn}-iddinam}, king of @wSN{Larsam}, your servant, says:
#lem: sum[beard]; mu[grow]; dumu[child]; Ningal[1]DN; sum[beard]; zagin[lapis lazuli]; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. (1:taka₄ la₂ {ŋiš!}si-ŋar an ki:1) ku₁₀-ku₁₀ zalag ŋa₂-ŋa₂#
#lem: taka[set aside]; la[hang]; siŋar[bolt]; an[sky]; ki[place]; kukkug[dark]; zalag[bright]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=7

:7v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) taka₄ si-ŋar
#lem: taka[set aside]; siŋar[bolt]

8. en saŋ-kal dili-a-ni pa e₃-a nam-mah-a-ni zag nu-sa₂
#lem: en[lord]; saŋkal[foremost]; dili[single]; pa[branch]; e[leave]; nammah[greatness]; zag[side]; sa[equal]
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. ur-saŋ dumu {d}nin-gal-e tud-da me saŋ keše₂ ur₄-ur₄
#lem: ursaŋ[warrior]; dumu[child]; Ningal[1]DN; utud[give birth (to)]; me[Being]; saŋ[head]; kešed[bind]; ur[gather]
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. diŋir zid nun! nam tar-tar-re a-a saŋ gig₂-ga lugal-ŋu₁₀-ur₂ u₂-na-de₃-tah
#lem: diŋir[deity]; zid[right]; nun[prince]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]; aya[father]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]; lugal[king]; tah[add]
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. {m}{d}suen-i-din-nam lugal larsam{ki}-ma arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: Siniddinam[1]RN; lugal[king]; Larsam[1]SN; arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=11

12. iri-zu larsam{ki}-ma šag₄-ge pad₃-da-zu niŋ₂-gig-ga im-ma-an-ak
#tr.en: Distress has been caused in your city @wSN{Larsam}, which you have chosen in your heart.
#lem: iri[city]; Larsam[1]SN; šag[heart]; pad[find]; niŋgig[that which is bad]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=12

13. sila daŋal ešemen ud zal-zal-la sig₉-ga (1:im-ma-an-sig₉:1)
#tr.en: The broad squares where days have been passed in merriment @varh[t3205.v3]{have been reduced to } @vart[t3205.v4,t3205.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} are left (?) in } silence.
#lem: sila[street]; daŋal[wide]; ešemen[skipping rope]; ud[sun]; zal[pass time]; sig[silent]; sig[put into]
#etcsl: line-id=13

:13v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) [...]-ŋar
#lem: ŋar[put]

14. erin₂! sag₉-ga-zu gu₂ ŋar-ŋar-ra gi gi-sig-ga-gin₇ si-il-si-le-de₃ ba#-an-til#-le-eš
#tr.en: Your commendable troops who were assembled have been annihilated (?) like reeds from a reed fence splitting apart.
#lem: erin[people]; sag[good]; gu[neck]; ŋar[put]; gi[reed]; gisig[reed fence]; sil[split]; til[complete]
#etcsl: line-id=14

15. ŋuruš!-zu še ud a₂-ba-gin₇ ab-gur₁₀ ba-an-šab-eš gurun gibil-gin₇ mu-X-dub₂#-uš
#tr.en: Your young men have been harvested like barley at the due time; they have been picked and have been plucked like ripened fruit (?).
#lem: ŋuruš[young adult male]; še[barley]; ud[sun]; a[time]; gur[reap]; šab[trim]; gurun[fruit]; gibil[new]; dub[tremble]
#etcsl: line-id=15

16. uŋ₃-ŋa₂ alan im-gin₇ im-ma-an-gul-lu-uš ni₂-bi-a ba-an-til#-[...]
#tr.en: The people have been smashed like terracotta figurines; they (?) have perished all together.
#lem: uŋ[people]; alan[image]; im[clay]; gul[destroy]; ni[self]; til[complete]
#etcsl: line-id=16

17. di₄-di₄-la₂ ur₂ ama-be₂-ne-ta ud hul ba-an-da-kar#-X X
#tr.en: An evil storm took away the little ones from the laps (?) of their mothers.
#lem: didila[small(er)]; ur[loin]; ama[mother]; ud[storm]; hulu[bad]; kar[flee]; X
#etcsl: line-id=17

18. uŋ₃-ŋa₂ ŋeštug! HAR-re muš₃-bi ba-an-kur₂ X [...]
#tr.en: The people ……; their appearance has been (?) changed.
#lem: uŋ[people]; ŋeštug[ear]; X; muš[face]; kur[different]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=18

19. erin₂ ka₃ an-ša-ša šu# bar-ra-am₃ kalam zid₂-gin₇ |KA×ŠU| e₃# [...]
#tr.en: Overwhelming troops have been set loose, …… the Land …… like flour.
#lem: erin[people]; kag[mouth]; šanšaša[cvve]; šu[hand]; bar[place outside]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; zid[flour]; X; e[leave]; X
#etcsl: line-id=19

20. šul {d}utu iri-za# larsam{ki}-ma lu₂-kur₂-gin₇ bar-ta ba-da-gub
#tr.en: O youthful @wDN{Utu}, like an enemy you stand aside from your city @wSN{Larsam}.
#lem: šul[youth]; Utu[1]DN; iri[city]; Larsam[1]SN; lukur[stranger]; bar[outside]; gub[stand]
#etcsl: line-id=20

21. kur elam{ki}-ma X{mušen}-gin₇ mah-bi# lu₂ uš₂-a nu-ŋal₂-la
#tr.en: The mountain land of @wGN{Elam} where there are no dead in great numbers (?) like ……,
#lem: kur[mountain(s)]; Elam[1]GN; X; mah[great]; lu[person]; uš[die]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=21

22. su-bir₄{ki} muru₉ dugud-da diŋir-re-e-ne ni₂ teŋ₃-ŋe₂₆ nu-zu#-a
#tr.en: and @wGN{Subir}, a heavy cloud,
#lem: Subir[1]GN; muru[rainstorm]; dugud[heavy]; diŋir[deity]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=22

23. ma-da-bi nu-ub-ta-be₄ ud-bi# nu-ŋal₂-la
#tr.en: which knows no reverence even towards the gods -- these districts have not been weakened;
#lem: mada[land]; be[diminish]; ud[sun]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#etcsl: line-id=23

24. (1:šimaški-e ki diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ nu-gig lukur nu-mu-da-il₂#-e:1)
#tr.en: their time has not yet come.
#lem: Šimaški[1]GN; ki[place]; diŋir[deity]; nugig[midwife]; lukur[priestess]; il[raise]
#etcsl: line-id=24

