#lem: Šimaški[1]GN; diŋir[deity]; nugig[midwife]; lukur[priestess]; il[raise]; zu[know]
:24v.1.2: ($1 other ms. has instead:$) šimaški ki diŋir-re-e-[ne] nu-gig nu-bar!-e nu-[...]
#lem: Šimaški[1]GN; ki[place]; diŋir[deity]; nugig[midwife]; nubar[female profession]; X

25. erin₂-a-ni u₂-gin₇ lu-lu-a numun-a-ni (1:daŋal-la:1)
#tr.en: @varh[t3205.v5]{The @wEN{Šimaškian} does not elect @fsux{nugig} or @fsux{lukur} priestesses for the places of the gods } @vart[t3205.v6,t3205.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} The @wEN{Šimaškian} knows neither his god nor those elected @fsux{nugig} and @fsux{lukur} priestesses } @vart[t3205.v7,t3205.v5]{@varn{1 other ms. has instead:} The @wEN{Šimaškian} …… neither the @fsux{nugig} nor the @fsux{nubar} priestesses for the places of the gods }. His soldiers are numerous like grass;
#lem: erin[people]; u[plant(s)]; lu[abundant]; numun[seed]; daŋal[wide]
#etcsl: line-id=25

:25v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) he₂-mah
#lem: mah[great]

26. za-lam-ŋar til₃-la ki diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄ nu-mu-un-zu-a
#tr.en: his seed @varh[t3205.v8]{is widespread } @vart[t3205.v9,t3205.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} is indeed exalted }. He who lives in tents,
#lem: zalamŋar[tent]; til[live (of a single person)]; ki[place]; diŋir[deity]; zu[know]
#etcsl: line-id=26

27. u₂-ma-am-gin₇-nam# u₅-a# (1:zid₂-eša# sizkur₂:1) nu-mu-un-zu-a
#tr.en: who does not know of the places of the gods:
